# 🐜 Ants vs. SomeBees

Ants vs. SomeBees is a Python tower-defense game inspired by the mechanics of *Plants vs. Zombies*. The objective is to defend your colony from waves of invading bees by strategically placing ants with unique abilities throughout the map.

Each ant serves a different purpose. Some generate resources, some attack enemies from a distance, and others provide defensive support. As the game progresses, players must balance resource management, positioning, and unit selection to stop increasingly challenging bee attacks before they reach the colony.

## Gameplay

* Deploy ants to defend tunnels from incoming bees.
* Generate food resources to place additional ants.
* Combine different ant types to create effective defenses.
* Survive all waves of bees to win the game.
* Prevent bees from reaching the colony's home base.

## Running the Game Locally

### Prerequisites

* Python 3 installed on your machine

### Launch the Game

From the project directory, run:

```bash
python3 gui.py
```

This will open the graphical interface and start the game.

## Project Structure

```text
ants.py      # Core game logic and insect classes
gui.py       # Graphical user interface
ucb.py       # Utility functions
assets/      # Images, sounds, and game assets
```

## Technologies Used

* Python 3
* Object-Oriented Programming
* Event-Driven Game Logic
* GUI-Based Simulation

Enjoy defending the colony!
